[Music]  I'm chair of the Scientific Advisory  Committee of the CFR program integrated  microbial biodiversity or imb what a  program like this does is bring people  together who would not necessarily  ordinarily talk to one another and to  throw out ideas that people haven't  thought about before and what that tends  to do is in many cases it totally  changes the way in which you think about  a problem and what you think you might  be able to do in a different way to  approach the problem the purpose of the  imv program is to get people that you  know think alike but about different  sorts of problems together and to give  us ways to look at problems from new  direction so for example I work on  eukaryotes these complex single cells  other people work on bacteria or viruses  well these things all live in the same  environment they all interact with each  other and it doesn't really do much good  to study one at a time in the  environment trying to understand the  function without studying all of them I  was one of the original members and in  the integrated microbial biodiversity  program but honestly I really wasn't  familiar with the community of  scientists that I was joining and so I  still have very fond memories of the  first meeting which was a planning  meeting and and my mind was blown by the  diversity of research that was going on  and through the meetings with other  members of the IMD I've been exposed to  the incredible diversity of biological  processes that happen in my crew with  eukaryotes and the idea that you can  really think of them as organisms that  have unique physiology unique ways of  interacting with the environment with  each other and that's really helped to  expand my perspectives in my own  research the cfri md program it's really  hard to pinpoint one specific area of my  research that it's impacted because I  really think it's changed the way that I  think and so in that way it changes  every  that I do in the IMD program I get to  work a lot with people that think about  evolution and typically in marine  microbiology we think a lot about marine  microbes and how they affect chemistry  think about their ecology which is why  you find certain organisms where you do  but the IMD program also thinks really  deeply about how organisms evolved and  putting my research my ecology research  and looking at it through this lens of  evolution has been really powerful how  does the world work you know how does  how does microbial life actually work  it's the problem with microbial life is  that the organisms are small you can't  see them but they're also massively  abundant and those and so complicated  right small massively abundant  incredibly important it's hard to put  that together you know so what people do  in the program is just take take slices  of that complexity from different places  and then at the meeting we can put it  together work it work through it and  then figure out you know heart to figure  out how it all fits together and to me  that's I mean what could be better than  that what's the most exciting problem in  biology because we're studying organisms  that haven't been well studied before  these are new discoveries and they're  they are generating questions that  people wouldn't have known to ask and so  that's what excites me about this  program it's really about discovery it's  not about incrementally improving our  knowledge about something that we  already knew about pretty well this is  about discovering something completely  new and unexpected and exciting and  opening up entirely new areas of  research we are studying the invisible  world from many different angles  I think the Edit value of the program is  this this combined big picture what do  protists will do bacteria and what do  virus is there and how these interact  these are studied separately until  actually I dare to say this program  implemented and I am not aware of any  other initiative that would lump all  this together so I believe that in the  end this will be the most important  outcome of this program to provide some  kind of integrated view of this tiny  world down there  [Music]  you

